=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play environment ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Environment screen proposed for slice 9,$
# drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host$
# (sudoers.Choose, Read, PlanFor), each change on the real$
# plan/apply engine (steps.Sudoers). Who ran hardn, the reader$
# of hardn's files and the plan's findings on the change are the$
# gallery's, unit (b)'s to build. Nothing on this machine$
# changes: every command and file is the fake's, and its record$
# is shown when play ends.$
$
# Environment hosts ############################################$
$
  Select a host$
$
   1) Debian 13$
      sudo, not kept$
   2) Ubuntu 26.04$
      sudo-rs, not kept$
   3) Alpine 3.24$
      doas through wheel$
   4) Alpine, rule$
      Treatment doas-rule$
   5) Alpine, setenv on wheel$
      The refusal followed$
   6) Alpine cloud image$
      wheel.conf read after$
   7) doas, overridden$
      hardn's rule, wheel.conf after$
   8) Proxmox VE 9$
      no sudo$
   9) Kept$
      hardn-env-alice there$
  10) Kept, keep only$
      Treatment item1-keep$
  11) Root login$
      Not run with sudo$
  12) hardn's grant$
      hardn-grant-alice there$
  13) Grant, no reader$
      An env-only Policy$
  14) Legacy file$
      /etc/sudoers.d/alice$
  15) Legacy, unread$
      Treatment legacy-hardn-only$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-15 or q]: 7$
$
# Info: environment/doas-overridden$
# web-01.example.net runs Alpine 3.23's cloud image, doas, as$
# the maintainer's VM; alice is in wheel, and the image's$
# /etc/doas.d/wheel.conf says permit nopass :wheel. alice ran$
# doas hardn. hardn's rule for alice keeps HARDN_CONFIG, but$
# wheel.conf's wins, so doas dropped it. Stopping rewrites a$
# rule that asks for alice's password.$
$
# Environment Variable Settings ################################$
$
# HARDN_CONFIG -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 alice$
  [ ] Under doas           Kept$
   -  /etc/doas.d/wheel.conf may override hardn's rule$
   -  Value                Not set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Under doas           Stop keeping HARDN_CONFIG$
                           [ ] Lockout risk$
   2) Guide                How to set HARDN_CONFIG$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# Environment hosts ############################################$
$
  Select a host$
$
   1) Debian 13$
      sudo, not kept$
   2) Ubuntu 26.04$
      sudo-rs, not kept$
   3) Alpine 3.24$
      doas through wheel$
   4) Alpine, rule$
      Treatment doas-rule$
   5) Alpine, setenv on wheel$
      The refusal followed$
   6) Alpine cloud image$
      wheel.conf read after$
   7) doas, overridden$
      hardn's rule, wheel.conf after$
   8) Proxmox VE 9$
      no sudo$
   9) Kept$
      hardn-env-alice there$
  10) Kept, keep only$
      Treatment item1-keep$
  11) Root login$
      Not run with sudo$
  12) hardn's grant$
      hardn-grant-alice there$
  13) Grant, no reader$
      An env-only Policy$
  14) Legacy file$
      /etc/sudoers.d/alice$
  15) Legacy, unread$
      Treatment legacy-hardn-only$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-15 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

